<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Enfield, London</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Enfield is a town in north <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, now the centre of a London borough. From 1816 to 1988 it was the site of the Royal Small Arms Factory at Enfield Lock, which made the Lee-Enfield rifle and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bren-light-machine-gun">Bren light machine gun</a> for the British armed forces.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/enfield-london.jpg" alt="Enfield, London" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christine Matthews · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St_Andrew%27s_Parish_Church,_Enfield_-_geograph.org.uk_-_187730.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
